  "Number": 19,
  "Question": "Suppose that \\(\\{a_n\\}\\) is an arithmetic sequence with \\[a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_{100} = 100\\] and \\[a_{101} + a_{102} + \\cdots + a_{200} = 200.\\] What is the value of \\(a_2 - a_1?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.0001\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.001\\)",
    "C": "\\(0.01\\)",
    "D": "\\(0.1\\)",
    "E": "\\(1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Let \\(d=a_2-a_1\\), the common difference. Each term in the second block is \\(100\\) positions after its corresponding term in the first block. Moving forward those \\(100\\) steps adds \\(d\\) exactly \\(100\\) times, so\n\\[\na_{k+100}-a_k=100d\n\\]\nfor \\(k=1,2,\\ldots,100\\).\n\nSubtracting the first block's sum from the second pairs all \\(100\\) corresponding terms. Therefore\n\\[\n200-100=100(100d)=10000d.\n\\]\nIt follows that\n\\[\na_2-a_1=d=\\frac{100}{10000}=\\boxed{0.01},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
